 The ramification of the above sentence gives us;
$\frac{1}{40} \sum_{i=1}^{40} age_i$ = 17.

Next, when we break the sum, we get;
$\frac{1}{40} \sum_{i=1}^{20} age_i $ + $\frac{1}{40} \sum_{i=21}^{35} age_i $ + $\frac{1}{40} \sum_{i=36}^{40} age_i$ = 17.
which is equivalent to;
$20(\frac{1}{20} \sum_{i=1}^{20} age_i) + 15(\frac{1}{15} \sum_{i=21}^{35} age_i) + 5(\frac{1}{5} \sum_{i=36}^{40} age_i) = 17$.
which further simplifies to;
$20*15 + 15*16 + 5*age_{adult} = 40*17$, using the ramification that on summing fractions equal to 1 they become equal to all their individual fractions.
Finally, solving we get:
$age_{adult} = 24.4$
